            provoked: ["*a boom so low you feel it in your ribs*"],
            idle: ["*it pecks at a fallen fruit*", "*bob* *bob*", "*a low rumble*"],
            hall: ["The people of the highlands raise my chicks, and they have a very healthy respect for my feet. So should you.", "I plant the forest. I eat the fruit, I walk a long way, and the seeds come out somewhere new. You are welcome."],
        ),
        ),
        // Their sheets are in the renderer (`targets/characters/howler_monkey.py`,
        // `green_iguana.py`, on `_art_cast_kit.py` and `_history_americas_kit.py`).
        // The heights are the heights of the boxes of the grid (`GRID3.md`).
        // The howler monkey: a mantled howler of the Olmec forest, dark with a
        // golden fringe. It keeps its distance and throws ripe fruit (the
        // `shoot` of a skirmisher): it stands up on its hind legs with the fruit
        // back over its shoulder first (its windup row). The fruit flies as a
